# Sync to Obsidian plugin copy

Whenever NarrativeLab source is changed, finish by building and deploying to the Obsidian vault plugin folder. Do not leave the plugin copy stale.

## Paths

- **Source**: NarrativeLab repo
- **Plugin copies** (copy `main.js`, `manifest.json`, `styles.css` to each):
  - `~/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-个人/My Library/.obsidian/plugins/narrative-lab`
  - `~/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-个人/My Library/.obsidianMac/plugins/narrative-lab`
  - `~/Documents/Obsidian/.obsidian/plugins/narrative-lab`

## Required steps after code changes

1. Edit source in the NarrativeLab repo (not the plugin folder).
2. Build: `npm run build` (esbuild production; deploys via `esbuild.config.mjs`).
3. Confirm deploy reached every plugin copy listed above (`main.js`, `styles.css`, `manifest.json` as applicable).
4. If deploy did not run, copy those built files into the plugin folder manually.

## Notes

- Prefer the build deploy path over hand-editing files under `.obsidian/plugins/narrative-lab` or `.obsidianMac/plugins/narrative-lab`.
- Set `NARRATIVE_LAB_DEPLOY_DIRS` to a path-delimited list of those plugin folders so `esbuild.config.mjs` copies build outputs to every copy.
- Remind the user to reload the plugin in Obsidian when a reload is needed to see changes.
